      <div style="margin-top:6pt;margin-bottom:252pt;margin-left:69.66pt;width:456pt;">
        <div style="width:456pt; line-height:12pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:bold;font-family:Times New Roman, Times, serif ;font-size:10pt;">
          <font style="letter-spacing:-0.2pt;">Compensation Actually Paid and Net Income (Loss)</font><font style="font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:0.2pt;"> </font>
        </div>
        <div style="text-indent:20pt; margin-top:8pt; width:456pt; line-height:12pt;font-family:Times New Roman, Times, serif ;font-size:10pt;">
          <font style="letter-spacing:0.2pt;">The following graph sets forth the relationship between Compensation Actually Paid to our PEO, the average of Compensation Actually Paid to our Non-PEO NEOs, and the Company&#8217;s net income (loss) over the two most recently completed fiscal&#160;years. </font>
        </div>
